  "description": "MUVYUZ crystallizes in the tetragonal crystal system with space group P 4 c c. Reported CIF formula moiety: C224 H216 Dy9 Fe16 O42 1-,C6 H16 N1 1+,H2 O1. From the CIF bond table, Dy2 (Dy) has 8 O neighbors; Dy1 (Dy) has 8 O neighbors; Dy3 (Dy) has 8 O neighbors; Fe3 (Fe) has 0 O neighbors; Fe4 (Fe) has 0 O neighbors; Fe2 (Fe) has 0 O neighbors; Fe1 (Fe) has 0 O neighbors; Dy4 (Dy) has 8 O neighbors; Dy5 (Dy) has 8 O neighbors; Fe5 (Fe) has 0 O neighbors; Fe6 (Fe) has 0 O neighbors; Fe7 (Fe) has 0 O neighbors; Fe8 (Fe) has 0 O neighbors; Dy6 (Dy) has 8 O neighbors; Dy7 (Dy) has 8 O neighbors; Fe9 (Fe) has 0 O neighbors; Fe10 (Fe) has 0 O neighbors; Fe11 (Fe) has 0 O neighbors; Fe12 (Fe) has 0 O neighbors; Dy8 (Dy) has 8 O neighbors; Dy9 (Dy) has 8 O neighbors; Fe13 (Fe) has 0 O neighbors; Fe14 (Fe) has 0 O neighbors; Fe15 (Fe) has 0 O neighbors; Fe16 (Fe) has 0 O neighbors. Oxygen-bridged metal-site graph: 20 pairs, 17 components; largest component is a network with cycles with three-dimensional metal-site arrangement. Computed bridged metal-metal separations span 3.580-5.114 Å (not direct metal-metal bonds). Computed M-O-M angles span 89.59-173.20°; individual values and O labels are in metal_framework.links. Article card reports molecular formula [Dy9(μ4-O)2(μ3-OH)8(μ-Fca)8(Fca)8][HN(C2H5)3]. Explicit grouped units in the article formula/name: 2 μ4-O (explicit grouped unit in article formula), 8 μ3-OH (explicit grouped unit in article formula).",
  "interpretation_limit": "Oxidation states, nuclearity, oxo/hydroxo bridging, core charge and ligand identities/counts require article/SI or manual verification; atom-site counts are asymmetric-unit counts, not molecular stoichiometry. Graph topology is limited to identity-symmetry bonds in the CIF table. Approximate shape is based only on bridge-unwrapped metal-site coordinates in the largest component; symmetry-related bonds or periodic structures require manual crystallographic review. Empirical formulas alone do not establish unique oxidation-state assignments or ligand connectivity; annotations above reproduce explicit structural notation only.",
